<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saphrax</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 376–380</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saphrax was a leader of the Greuthungi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alatheus">Alatheus</a>, led part of the people across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> into Roman territory in 376 after the Hunnic invasion. Together with the Tervingi of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fritigern">Fritigern</a> they fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-376-382">Gothic War</a>, and the sudden arrival of their cavalry decided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adrianople">Battle of Adrianople</a> in 378. The historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammianus-marcellinus">Ammianus Marcellinus</a> is the main source for his career.</p></div>
